            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Russian for a bachelor, then the Russian for a master’s graduate."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: доклад",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "доклад (doklád) — \"a talk, a paper (given aloud)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "На конференции я делаю доклад. Na konferéntsii ya délayu doklád. I am giving a talk at the conference."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine. A prepared talk, or a report to a superior: доклад (doklád) начальнику."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "доклад (doklád) is built on докладывать \"to report\", from до- and класть \"to lay\", inherited from Proto-Slavic klasti: to lay a matter before someone."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
